<% content_for :title, "Standard Deviation Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Standard Deviation calculator page (frontend issue #191; spec #190, DESIGN.md BLEND). A
  VARIABLE-LENGTH LIST input (the Mean·Median·Mode·Range pattern — a single textarea the
  user types a comma/space/newline-separated list into) paired with a POPULATION/SAMPLE
  MODE picker that selects the variance denominator (÷ n vs ÷ n−1).

  Submit model: a plain server-rendered <form> posting inputs[...] to the §4 endpoint over
  Turbo (Accept: turbo-stream → the #result region re-renders in place). It works with NO
  JS — the server parses the list, validates the chosen mode, and re-renders the result.
  There is no Stimulus controller: the mode picker is a native radio <fieldset> whose
  .peer:checked baseline paints the active half without JS, so nothing client-side is
  needed.

  Mode-picker presentation (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"): N = 2 modes with short labels
  (Population / Sample, ≤12 chars) → the SEGMENTED CONTROL (the connected horizontal track,
  the same vocabulary as BMI's US|Metric and Percentage's Increase|Decrease), NOT the
  .mode-option list (reserved for N ≥ 4 or multi-word labels) and NOT a <select>. Each half
  carries a one-line "÷ n" / "÷ n−1" helper naming the denominator it selects, so the
  difference between the two modes reads in text, not by position alone (DESIGN.md §6).

  Layout (DESIGN.md §3): an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr), one column on
  mobile (mobile-first). Spacing — segmented halves tight (gap-1, Affix tier), the major
  blocks (mode → list → submit) → mt-8 (Section tier), column gutter / card padding →
  gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout tier).
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Math</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Standard Deviation Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Enter a list of numbers and get the
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">standard deviation</span>,
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">variance</span> and
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">mean</span>, plus the count and sum. Choose
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">population</span> or
    <span class="font-semibold text-ink">sample</span> to set the variance denominator.
    Separate values with commas, spaces, or new lines. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/standard_deviation", scope: :inputs, method: :post do |f| %>

      <%# Mode picker — SEGMENTED CONTROL (DESIGN.md §4 picker rule: N=2, short labels). One
          connected, bg-tinted, bordered track; the two modes are halves (.direction-pill)
          tight on the Affix tier (gap-1 — parts of one control). The active half lifts to
          surface white via .peer:checked (no-JS baseline). Native radio <fieldset>/<legend>
          posting a single-select inputs[mode]; population is checked by default (it is
          defined for any n ≥ 1, the safe default — sample needs n ≥ 2). %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="field-label">Data set</legend>
        <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
          <% [["population", "Population"], ["sample", "Sample"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
            <%= f.radio_button :mode, value, checked: i.zero?, class: "peer sr-only" %>
            <%= f.label :mode, text, value: value, class: "direction-pill" %>
          <% end %>
        </div>
        <%# The denominator each mode selects — named in text so the two modes are
            distinguishable beyond the toggle's position (DESIGN.md §6). %>
        <p class="mt-1.5 text-[11px] leading-snug text-faint">
          Population divides by <span class="font-semibold text-muted tabular-nums">n</span>;
          sample divides by <span class="font-semibold text-muted tabular-nums">n − 1</span>
          (sample needs at least 2 values).
        </p>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Values — the variable-length list input as a <textarea> (the MMR pattern): a long
          list of numbers is the headline interaction, so it needs room to wrap and stay
          readable (DESIGN.md §3 "let pages breathe"). It carries the .field-input vocabulary
          (border-input, focus ring → accent, tabular-nums) so figures align as typed.
          Section tier above (mt-8). %>
      <div class="mt-8">
        <%= f.label :values, "Values", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_values" %>
        <p id="values_hint" class="mt-1 text-xs leading-relaxed text-muted">
          Separated by commas, spaces, or new lines — e.g.
          <span class="font-semibold text-ink tabular-nums">10, 12, 23, 23, 16</span>
        </p>
        <%= f.text_area :values, id: "inputs_values", rows: 5,
              placeholder: "10, 12, 23, 23, 16, 23, 21, 16",
              "aria-describedby": "values_hint",
              class: "field-input mt-2 resize-y leading-relaxed" %>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; the primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target; aria-live so the answer is announced) ── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
